## 6. do the path-carrying commands (doc / design / evidence / deployment) persist absolute paths?
-- doc add --
harness doc — Document registry — the artifacts a gate reviews.

Subcommands:
  upsert --id <DOC-x> --path <p> --phase <P> [--refs <ids>] [--url <url>]
                                  Register or update a document. --refs links it to ledger nodes (RTM traceability).
  url <DOC-x> <artifact-url>      Attach a published artifact URL to a document.
  submit <DOC-x>                  Submit a document for review (pins its hash).
  approve <DOC-x>                 Approve a submitted document.
  revise <DOC-x> [--path <p>]     Revise an approved document (supersedes the old version).
  stale                           List approved documents whose content no longer matches the pinned hash.
  list                            Print the whole registry as JSON.
-- design --help --
harness design — Claude Design canvas link — UX nodes, sync and baselines.

Subcommands:
  link --ux <UX-x> --url <canvas-url> [--artboard <name>]
                                  Link a UX node to a canvas artboard.
  sync <UX-x> --from <file>       Sync fetched canvas content into the ledger.
  inventory --from <file>         Extract a component inventory from canvas content.
  baseline <UX-x> --png <file>    Record a baseline screenshot for a UX node.
  html <UX-x>                     Render the linked artboard as standalone HTML.
  list                            Print all canvas links as JSON.
-- evidence? --
  status          Print current phase, active wave, gates and backtrack as JSON.
  doctor          Diagnose state vs journal and policy drift; --repair replays state, --accept-policy re-pins the policy baseline (needs HARNESS_ACCEPT_POLICY=1 — humans only).
  phase <sub>     Move to a phase. Only an approved gate opens the next phase.
  gate <sub>      Phase gates — submit artifacts, then a human approves.
  wave <sub>      Waves — the unit of build work, with a written instruction sheet.
  node <sub>      Design ledger nodes — the things waves are allowed to implement.
  trace           Trace a design node to the waves and documents that reference it.
  report <sub>    Rendered views over the ledger, registry and gates.
  doc <sub>       Document registry — the artifacts a gate reviews.
  adr <sub>       Architecture decision records tied to phase gates.
  design <sub>    Claude Design canvas link — UX nodes, sync and baselines.
  tokens <sub>    Design tokens — generate, lint raw values, swap themes.
  evidence <sub>  Visual evidence for UX waves — spec, check and packet.
  loop <sub>      Wave execution loop — next work, attempts, briefs, escalation.
  ship <sub>      Ship track — defect ledger, deployments, final verdict.
  profile <sub>   Stack profile — what "build", "test", "deploy" mean here.
  usage <sub>     Usage tier guidance for long sessions.
  backtrack       Officially go back to an earlier phase (the only way to edit approved design).
  migrate         Detect hand-rolled hooks/skills that would double-fire with the harness.

